Things that needed to be followed when developing the project:
• For administrative functionalities, the admin user should not be required to update the
system via a database, files, WordPress admin page, Django Administration page, etc...
Instead, you need to develop a dedicated admin page where they can add movies, delete
them, view system status, and perform other tasks directly. You must develop a graphical
interface that allows the admin to make such changes.
• For the programming portion, implementing the lottery ticket claiming center
functionality is optional. To keep the program short, you may omit all features associated
with claiming prizes above $599. However, if these features are applicable to your UML
diagrams, they must be included.
• Always keep a backup of your code in case it gets deleted.
• This is a team project, so the entire team must verify each other's work. If an issue is
found in a teammate's contribution, it is your responsibility to work with them to correct
it. Record such efforts in the team contribution table. Failure to resolve project issues will
result in point deductions for the entire team, as it reflects a lack of understanding by all
members.
• If you encounter an issue with a team member not participating, notify your instructor
immediately after class. The instructor will then communicate with the student to resolve
the issue or, if necessary, remove them from the group. Do not wait until the last week to
report such problems; doing so makes the situation your responsibility.
• A team member who keeps promising to deliver work at the end but does not show any
progress is a major red flag. If a team member is not showing progress, it likely means
they are not doing their part. You should speak with your instructor right away rather
than waiting until the last few weeks.
• Not completing work on time due to group issues is the responsibility of each team
member. Therefore, it is essential to communicate with the instructor immediately to
address and resolve any group-related problems.
• Waiting until the end and complaining that other team members did not assign you any
work or contact you is not an excuse. This will result in a lower grade or even a grade of
zero for not completing any work. Completing your work promptly is the responsibility
of each individual team member.
• Please note that the “Local and Global Impacts” question is worth only 5 points. If a team
member works solely on this part, they will receive only 5 points for Phase 2. All team
members must contribute equally to earn an equal grade. Simply proofreading the
documents or attending meetings does not count as an equal contribution to work.
